name: Focused Review survives resize and offers exact current-observation recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 rows 1-500 of 800 | first-page
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 25 501-800/800 | later-page
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | open-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: confirmed | opened-source
expect: DECISION SOURCE
expect-echo-within: 300 retained-resize-draft
live-snap: retained-draft
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART replace
require-live-snap: 25 earlier observation | historical-source
expect: open F-0601 inspect current
expect: retained-resize-draft
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | historical-detail-60x20
expect: earlier observation
expect: retained-resize-draft
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | historical-detail-40x12
expect: earlier observation
expect: retained-resize-draft
ask: Does narrowing preserve the historical detail and draft, with the warning distinguishing an earlier observation from a filter issue?
keys: C-u
nav-mode:
keys: g
keys: NPage
live-snap: historical-recovery-control
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 501-800/800 | narrow-list-return
expect: Synthetic continuity candidate 0727
expect: earlier F-0601
resize: 120x36
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | current-inspection-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Owned later source; never executed. | current-observation
expect-not: shows an earlier observation
submit: decision deferred J145 current observation deliberately deferred
nav-mode:
keys: g
require-live-snap: 25 J145 current observation deliberately deferred | current-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART decided
ask: Does the displayed inspect-current command explicitly select the new observation before a decision, preserving the earlier decision?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | current-detail-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | current-detail-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | current-detail-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | current-detail-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | current-detail-40x12
expect: F-0601
keys: NPage
live-snap: current-decision-page-1
keys: NPage
live-snap: current-decision-page-2
expect: recorded: deferred
resize: 120x36
live-snap: expanded-reading-position
keys: g
require-live-snap: 20 J145 current observation deliberately deferred | expanded-two-pane
expect: 501-800/800
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 501-800/800 | expanded-list-return
ask: Does detail remain focused without an extra Enter at narrow sizes, and does expanding restore the list/detail layout with normal reading and return controls?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 25 rows 1-500 of 800 | recovered-first
nav-mode:
keys: C-n
require-live-snap: 25 501-800/800 | recovered-later
resize: 40x12
paste-file: @ART/open.txt
require-live-snap: 15 open F- | recovered-open-draft
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SELECTED FINDING | recovered-narrow-detail
nav-mode:
keys: NPage
keys: NPage
require-live-snap: 20 recorded: deferred | recovered-narrow-decision
keys: q
require-live-snap: 20 501-800/800 | recovered-narrow-list
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finding_continuity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart retain both observations and decisions, with narrow detail and list access and no new provider or scanner work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
